{
  "contract": "chat_receipt_projection_v4",
  "note": "DEV-030. Generated from the server's own _operation_projection; the iOS client reads this file rather than a copy. Both sides must agree case by case, because the client's only reason to say 已写入 is a record_id in one of these bodies, and an indeterminate/manual-review result must not release the durable idempotency slot. v3 adds query_result: a succeeded finance.query_expenses receipt carries the whitelisted projection plus a deterministic answer fallback, and the client renders it as a structured card rather than prose. v4 pins query_evidence_tools: the server derives it from the IR (governed read whose output contract is the expense query projection), and the client holds its hard-coded `tool == \"finance.query_expenses\"` check against it, so a rename or a second governed query fails both suites before it reaches a user.",
